    "summary": "Cherry Gulch was a ranch-style therapeutic boarding school in Emmett, Idaho, for boys who were about 10 to 14 years old when they enrolled. It offered schooling along with weekly therapy for students with learning differences and emotional or behavioral challenges. California was certified to place students there as an out-of-state nonpublic school. California's school directory lists it as closed as of May 24, 2025."
